<!-- C13-tie-not-adjacent (added by the G0 fixer, not by the independent author): bar 1 = G4 eighth with <tie type="start"/>, then F#4 eighth, then G4 quarter with <tie type="stop"/> (the tie skips a note, as in catalog/method/sonatina/010 bar 21); bar 2 = E5 half with <tie type="start"/>, a quarter rest, then E5 quarter with <tie type="stop"/> (the stop lands after a gap, as in samples/prelude-fragment bars 6-7). A tie joins a note only to the next note of the same pitch that starts where it ends, so every note here is its own key press. -->
